      "side": 1,
      "message": "This creates a dependency from vnet core to the PIPE plugin, which is not an allowed layering direction: plugins may depend on vnet, but vnet must never depend on a plugin. Moving the implementation does not resolve that while vnet still owns `VNET_SW_INTERFACE_TYPE_PIPE` and contains PIPE-specific branches.\n\nCould this use a generic device-owned child-interface abstraction instead? Parent resolution and lifecycle should use generic child-interface semantics, P2P behavior can come from `VNET_HW_INTERFACE_CLASS_FLAG_P2P`, and a generic device-class L2-mode operation would let PIPE own its state without the Ethernet callback registry.\n\nThe existing `IF_API_TYPE_PIPE` value may remain solely as wire-API compatibility metadata, but there should be no PIPE-specific runtime type or control flow in vnet.",
      "revId": "6e74125cb7cbfc3018924c7976855f3102092806",
